### Muraka API - reference requests
###
### Every call a mobile client makes, in the order it makes them. Runnable from
### VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP Client, or by translating to curl.
###
### Start the stack first:
###   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d
###   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec api seed -sightings 500

@host = http://localhost:8090
@contentType = application/json

### --- is it up? -------------------------------------------------------------

GET {{host}}/healthz

###

GET {{host}}/readyz

### --- sign in ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Capture accessToken and refreshToken from the response. The refresh token is
### single-use: store the new one on every refresh.

# @name login
POST {{host}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "diver@muraka.test",
  "password": "muraka-diver-2026"
}

###

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refreshToken}}

### Register instead (new accounts are always contributors)

POST {{host}}/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "new.diver@muraka.test",
  "password": "at-least-ten-characters",
  "displayName": "New Dive Guide"
}

### --- profile and totals ----------------------------------------------------

GET {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- submit a sighting -----------------------------------------------------
### Step 1: metadata. `id` is a client-generated UUIDv7 and is the idempotency
### key. Replay this exact request: the second call returns 200, not 201, and
### creates nothing. That is what makes the offline queue safe to retry.

POST {{host}}/v1/sightings
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "id": "018f3c2a-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
  "lat": 4.1755,
  "lon": 73.5093,
  "locationSource": "gps",
  "locationAccuracyM": 8.0,
  "depthM": 7.5,
  "capturedAt": "2026-08-18T09:14:22Z",
  "note": "North side of the thila, patchy pale tissue",
  "selfAssessedCondition": "bleached"
}

### Step 2: one call per photograph. Also idempotent, on photoId.
### Point `file` at a real JPEG on disk before running this.

POST {{host}}/v1/sightings/018f3c2a-0000-7000-8000-000000000001/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----MurakaBoundary

------MurakaBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photoId"

018f3c2b-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
------MurakaBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="reef.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./reef.jpg
------MurakaBoundary--

### --- read it back ----------------------------------------------------------
### Poll this after upload. Status walks pending_photos -> processing ->
### awaiting_verification, then verified or rejected once an expert decides.
### `photos[].prediction` carries patchGrid and the patches array for the overlay.

GET {{host}}/v1/sightings/018f3c2a-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### My sightings, newest first. Contributors only ever see their own.

GET {{host}}/v1/sightings?limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Photograph bytes. Needs the bearer token, so an image loader has to be
### configured with the auth header - a bare URL will 401.

GET {{host}}/v1/photos/018f3c2b-0000-7000-8000-000000000001/image
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- token refresh ---------------------------------------------------------
### On 401: refresh once, store BOTH new tokens, retry the original request.
### Serialise this - two concurrent refreshes will kill the session, because the
### second presents an already-used token.

POST {{host}}/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### --- reference data -------------------------------------------------------
### Public: usable before sign-in, e.g. to centre a map.

GET {{host}}/v1/atolls

###

GET {{host}}/v1/sites
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- sign out --------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{host}}/v1/auth/logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### --- delete the account ---------------------------------------------------
### Anonymises rather than erases: sightings survive as scientific record with
### the personal link severed. Say so in the confirmation dialog.

DELETE {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- error shapes worth handling ------------------------------------------

### 422 with per-field detail
POST {{host}}/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short",
  "displayName": ""
}

### 401 without a token
GET {{host}}/v1/sightings

### 403 - a contributor reaching for a researcher endpoint
GET {{host}}/v1/verifications/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- researcher endpoints (not used by the contributor app) ---------------
### Included so mobile work can verify its own submissions end to end.

# @name researcherLogin
POST {{host}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "researcher@muraka.test",
  "password": "muraka-research-2026"
}

###

@researcherToken = {{researcherLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Review queue: lowest model confidence first

GET {{host}}/v1/verifications/queue?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{researcherToken}}

### Record a decision. confirmed/corrected need `label`; rejected needs
### `rejectReason`. Appends to history - the model's prediction is preserved.

POST {{host}}/v1/sightings/018f3c2a-0000-7000-8000-000000000001/verification
Authorization: Bearer {{researcherToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "decision": "confirmed",
  "label": "bleached",
  "comment": "Consistent with the surrounding colony"
}

### Map data. Clustered below zoom 11, individual points above.

GET {{host}}/v1/map/points?zoom=7&bbox=71.8,-1.2,74.2,7.4
Authorization: Bearer {{researcherToken}}

### Condition over time

GET {{host}}/v1/trends?bucket=month
Authorization: Bearer {{researcherToken}}
